---
/* The seasonal overlay's hero pieces: two top corners, a flock that hangs or
   flies above the hero art, and a band of snow along the hero's top edge.
   Empty elements whose pictures come from `season.css`, which draws them only
   under `html[data-season]`, so a page with no season active fetches no
   picture and paints nothing here. The layer sits under `main`'s top edge,
   which is the hero's, and every piece is placed in space the hero leaves
   empty; the section-edge pieces and the character are pseudo-elements in
   `season.css` rather than markup here, because they belong to sections this
   component does not render. */
import '../styles/season.css';
---

<div class="season-layer" aria-hidden="true">
	<i class="season-corner season-corner-start"></i>
	<i class="season-corner season-corner-end"></i>
	<i class="season-flock"></i>
	<i class="season-snow"></i>
</div>
